The doorbell rings at eight o'clock.
I open the door.
Asha is standing outside with her dog, Moti.
Moti wags his tail enthusiastically.
"Come in, Asha!" I say with a smile.
We sit at the dining table.
I serve the hot food on the plates.
I have made a special Mexican dish, but using Indian spices.
Asha takes the first bite and smiles.
"Maya, this food is incredibly tasty!" she says.
"Thank you," I reply happily.
Moti is sitting under the table.
He looks at me and begs for food.
"No, Moti, this is spicy," I tell him.
Then Asha asks me about my plans for tomorrow.
"What are you doing tomorrow, on Sunday?" she asks.
"I am going to rest at home," I say.
We talk for a long time about our weekend.
I feel truly settled here in Mumbai now.
